        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "Assume AC_omega. Let I be an open interval, t* in I, p:I->R continuous and C1 off t* with one-sided limits p(t*+-), p'(t*+-) existing. Put p'_reg = p' off t*, [p]=p(t*+)-p(t*-). Then p and p'_reg are locally integrable and (u_p)' = u_{p'_reg} + [p] delta_{t*} in D'(I): for every test function phi, -int p phi' dlambda = int p'_reg phi dlambda + [p] phi(t*).",
        "strategy": "Local integrability from finitely many discontinuities plus the Riemann-Lebesgue comparison; two half-interval integrations by parts of the C1 extensions, assembled with a.e. equality and linearity.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
