        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "Assume AC_omega. Let x_i be continuous on I and C2 off t* with one-sided velocity limits v_i^+-; let F_i continuous and J in R^3. Adopt the isolated reciprocal impulse model: m_i x_i''=F_i off t*, and for every C_c^inf vector test Phi, -int <p_i,Phi'> dlambda = int <F_i,Phi> dlambda +- <J,Phi(t*)>. Then (a) m_1(v_1^+-v_1^-)=J and m_2(v_2^+-v_2^-)=-J, so total momentum is continuous across t*; (b) given the restitution law v_2^+-v_1^+=-e(v_2^--v_1^-), 0<=e<=1, the post-impulse velocities are uniquely V + (m_2/M)e(v_2^--v_1^-) and V - (m_1/M)e(v_2^--v_1^-) with V the centre-of-mass velocity; (c) the kinetic-energy change is -(1-e^2)mu||v_2^--v_1^-||^2/2 <= 0.",
        "strategy": "Apply the scalar jump lemma to each momentum component and compare with the model pairing to get the jumps; solve the linear system for the post-impulse velocities; use the two-body kinetic splitting with the common centre-of-mass velocity.",
